  {
   "slug": "speech-824725",
   "speaker": "Mathias Cormann",
   "party": "Liberal",
   "state": "federal",
   "date": "2013-06-20",
   "stage_hint": null,
   "brief": "The coalition will not oppose the International Monetary Agreements Amendment Bill 2013, which authorises a loan of up to 4.61 billion special drawing rights (approximately A$6.8 billion) to the IMF under a bilateral agreement. Senator Xenophon supported the bill but raised concerns about IMF transparency and conditions, referencing criticisms by economist Jeffrey Sachs and journalist Ross Greenwood, and asked for scrutiny of how the loan would be used."
  }
